# ~/.config/t3flare/dev.env: a workstation's Deployment settings and deploy credentials (docs/deploy.md).
# Copy it there, `chmod 600` it, and fill in the values; never commit the filled-in file. stage.ts reads the keys it
# needs from it (a value in the environment wins); `ci:setup` sources it whole. Don't source it into your shell.

# --- Deployment settings (docs/deploy.md): no defaults; a deploy without one stops and names it ---

# The account's Access team, <team>.cloudflareaccess.com. Every deploy.
T3FLARE_ACCESS_TEAM_DOMAIN=
# The Owner, the one person Access admits to the admin routes. Every deploy (a repository secret in CI).
T3FLARE_OWNER_EMAIL=
# The account's workers.dev subdomain, the <x> in <x>.workers.dev. Every deploy.
T3FLARE_WORKERS_DEV_SUBDOMAIN=
# The Deployment repository, owner/name, which ci:setup and github-app:setup configure.
GITHUB_REPOSITORY=
# The id (32 hex characters) of the zone prod's custom domain is in. ci:setup only.
T3FLARE_DOMAIN_ZONE_ID=
# The repository (owner/name) the acceptance test and the stage scripts clone and push to; the GitHub App must be
# installed on it. ci:setup sets it on the `bump` environment.
T3FLARE_FIXTURE_REPO=
# The zone (a hostname) a test stage's stand-in laptop gets its hostname in. Only for a deploy with T3FLARE_STANDIN=1.
# T3FLARE_STANDIN_ZONE=
# prod's update target (owner/name, the Deployment repository), for ci:setup to set on the `prod` environment. stage.ts
# never reads it from here; unset, prod has no in-app Update.
# T3FLARE_UPDATE_REPO=
# prod's custom domain. stage.ts takes it from the shell only, for a prod deploy (any other stage is refused while it is
# set); ci:setup takes it from the shell or from here.
# T3FLARE_DOMAIN=

# --- Deploy credentials and options (not Deployment settings) ---

# The GitHub App (ADR-0013), written by `pnpm --filter @t3flare/infra run github-app:setup`. Every deploy.
# T3FLARE_GITHUB_APP_ID=
# T3FLARE_GITHUB_APP_PRIVATE_KEY=
# The stages' Model endpoints, one or a JSON list (docs/model-endpoints.md, "The stages' Model endpoints"). Optional.
# T3FLARE_MODEL_ENDPOINT=
# ci:setup: prod's bootstrap and admin tokens file, when running from a worktree (default:
# apps/environment/.alchemy/stages/prod.env.json in this checkout).
# T3FLARE_PROD_ENV_FILE=
